  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Defense Threat Reduction (DOD)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kazakhstan Veterinary Epidemiology Training - USDA implemented a trade capacity building program to strengthen Kazakhstans capacity to comply with World Organization for Animal Health guidelines for surveillance, detection, diagnosis and reporting of notifiable diseases. Kazakhstan technical level government personnel have already taken basic veterinary epidemiology trainings. In order to assess and inform the development of Kazakhstans plans for meeting practical veterinary epidemiological needs within their animal health system, this training presented high level officials and decision makers a basic background in epidemiology to educate them on the role of epidemiology in surveillance and disease control. This training will be followed by a discussion of Kazakhstans plans for how to integrate practical veterinary epidemiology into their animal health system. Findings and outcomes from the discussion will inform USDAs plans for training and capacity building programming in the future.</narrative>
  </description>
